Vendored from a shallow clone of the v2.1 branch at the commit above.
Includes src/, COPYRIGHT and dynasm/ (required by src/msvcbuild.bat).
Omitted documentation, tests, Makefiles, ignore files and console build scripts.
The original source files and msvcbuild.bat are otherwise unchanged.

The root .relver contains the commit's Unix timestamp, 1794386141, instead
of git's unexpanded $Format:%ct$ placeholder. Without a .git directory,
msvcbuild.bat copies this into src/luajit_relver.txt and genversion.lua
writes LuaJIT 2.1.1794386141 into the generated src/luajit.h.

build.ps1 copies this directory to build/native/luajit-src before building.
Only that copy is modified. In msvcbuild.bat:
- Add /MT and /DLUAJIT_ENABLE_CHECKHOOK to LJCOMPILE.
- Replace /MD with /MT (and consequently /MDd with /MTd).
- Make the BAD and FAIL labels exit /b 1 instead of falling through END.
In lj_err.c:
- LJ_EXCODE 0xe24c4a00 becomes 0x624c4a00 (informational severity).
It calls vcvars64.bat, then msvcbuild.bat static in the copied src directory,
and copies src/lua51.lib to build/native/luajit.lib.
The release static library uses the MSVC static multithreaded CRT (/MT),
matching md4c and notifications. CHECKHOOK permits asynchronous hooks to
interrupt JIT-compiled loops. No Lua 5.2 compatibility mode is enabled.

Error unwinding stays external (Windows SEH, upstream's Windows default).
Every lua_error, including one a pcall catches, is a RaiseException call.
With upstream's error-severity code, Odin's test runner treats it as a
fatal signal on a test thread and crash tooling may report it. The
informational code avoids both; LuaJIT matches its own exceptions by the
same LJ_EXCODE macro, so nothing else changes.
LUAJIT_NO_UNWIND (internal unwinding) was rejected: on Windows x64 the
interpreter frame saves only rbx, rsi, rdi and rbp (vm_x64.dasc X64WIN
saveregs; the -D NO_UNWIND DynASM flag only changes the POSIX layout), so
lj_vm_unwind_c returns from lua_pcall with r12-r15 and xmm6-xmm15 left as
the raising C function set them. A probe built with /DLUAJIT_NO_UNWIND and
-D NO_UNWIND returned from lua_pcall with all of r12-r15 corrupted; the
default build preserved them.
Neither unwinder runs Odin defers in the frames it unwinds, so CFunctions
must release what they own before raising.

The rebuild stamp is this VERSION file. Update it whenever changing the
vendored revision, local source patches or native build options.
